    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d151">

                <pb facs="0160" n="150" sameAs="frus:frus1941v05/pg150"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">792.94/108: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Thailand</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Grant</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bangkok</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-05-10T17:00:00+07:00">May 10, 1941—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received May 10—10:45 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>267. The British Minister informed me this morning very confidentially that he
                    has received most reliable information to the effect that the Japanese Minister
                    at Bangkok has reported to his Government that preparations are being made for a
                        <hi rendition="#italic">coup d’etat</hi> in Thailand with a view to
                    organizing a new pro-Japanese Government. The British Minister said he had
                    reported the matter to the Deputy Minister of Foreign Affairs for transmission
                    to the Prime Minister.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Grant</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
